UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|We might make 6 if East did not lead a major suit because North could discard the losing spade on a diamond.|
PG| ***** 41 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I personally like playing that 3 level bids over 1NT are natural slam tries. But most don't play that. They have all sorts of weird usages for 3 level bids. Some like to play 3@C is |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=puppetstayman,Puppet Stayman^*N|CP||FP||at| over 1N to find out whether partner has a 5 card major. That is actually quite popular and that is perfectly fine.|
PG| ***** 42 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BNorth: ^*nSo even though counting points supported slam it was not there?|
PG| ***** 43 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Yes. |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=bergenhandevaluation,Bergen Hand Evaluation^*N|CP||FP||at| supported that slam was possible with only 27-29 HCP, since you have 12 HCP and I have 15-17|
PG| ***** 44 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|But it was quite possible we are missing 2 aces.|
PG| ***** 45 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BWest: ^*nCould you transfer and then go to RCKB?|
PG| ***** 46 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|If you play |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| and 4 way transfers.|
PG| ***** 47 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In that scenario, North could bid 2@S (club transfer) and then over whatever I bid (2N without a club honor but 3@C here because I have the @CA) North could then bid 4@D |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=kickback,Kickback^*N|CP||FP||at| RKCB and end up in 5@C.|
PG| ***** 48 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|So if you play 3@C over 1N is Puppet Stayman, then 1N-2@S-3@C-4@D-4N (2 keys no @CQ)-5@C is actually the best auction|
PG| ***** 49 ***** |


