qx|A4|st||rh||ah|Board 4 IMPs   -   May 15, 2024|pn|hondo717,Honeydog3,aspiring,Toasterln|
md|2SK86532H865D7CKJ8,SAQJHT32D93CA9632,STHJ4DAKQT542CQ74,S974HAKQ97DJ86CT5|sv|b|
mb|P|mb|1D|mb|1H|mb|1S?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|West can show a limit raise with 3 card support as 2@D would show a 3-card limit raise and 2@S would show a 4-card limit raise. Many don't play that but it is a good thing to play. Absent that, you sometimes cue bid with 3-card support even though you like to have 4 to make a limit raise.|
PG| ***** 51 ***** |


mb|2D?|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|North, with a self sufficient suit, really wants to play in diamonds even if I am short. So the correct bid is 3@D. If North doubled 2@D, that would still show real diamonds but a somewhat weaker suit, not willing to unilaterally play 3@D.
|
