UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|It turns out that 3@H makes but I 100% agree with East's pass of 3@D. With a flat hand and 8 card fit, 3@H is anti |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at|. So this is one of the few hands where |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| fails. It does happen but very rarely. So if you use the |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=lott,Law of Total Tricks^*N|CP||FP||at| to determine how high you should compete, you will be right 95% of the time. You even bid better than those experts who ignore the law of total tricks.|
PG| ***** 66 ***** |


