UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Let us discuss the best way to play the hand. North has 9 sure tricks, 8 hearts and a club. The best play is to hope East holds the AJ of spades or KJ of spades and lead spades twice towards dummy intending to play the 10 if East plays low. And that works as it turns out.|
PG| ***** 84 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|In this fashion Declarer loses 2 spades but not 3. The way it was played Declarer lost control of the hand and ended up losing a diamond because Declarer was out of trump. North should overtake the @HK in hand hand, draw trump, and play a spade to the 10. |
PG| ***** 85 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Then Declarer endup only losing 2 spades not 3, taking 8 hearts, 1 club, and 1 spade for 10 tricks. Suit combinations of which this is an example are very hard to learn because there are so many variations.|
PG| ***** 86 ***** |


